  "summary": "Skills collection with benign install/verify scripts",
  "details": "Package bundles a collection of 'skills' (helper scripts, templates, documentation) under bundled-skills/. a static rule fired on keyword co-occurrence in several of these bundled files, but the matches correspond to legitimate behaviors: a Python scraper that uses ping/HTTP verbs against a target site referenced by its own name (junta-leiloeiros), an rclone installer script that fetches from the official rclone.org domain, a loki-mode benchmark runner, and a youtube-notetaker verification script making GET requests to documented endpoints. No installer-secret paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser stores, env scraping) are read, no attacker-controlled or anonymous host is contacted, and the scripts are inert data under bundled-skills/ rather than code auto-executed by npm lifecycle hooks or top-level module load. The static hits are keyword-proximity false positives on legitimate helper scripts shipped as skill content.",
